Chapter: Unicode Bytes Roundtrip

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 Every fixture that exercised this pair before was tier 0, so the pair could
 round-trip ASCII and nothing else and stay green (L-CONSTRUCT). The rows below
 straddle all four CCE bands. The unit columns are the framing cce-encode's
 arithmetic mandates, computed by hand rather than copied from a run, so a
 change that moves both the encoder and this file cannot agree with itself.

 The buried arm is the control for a positional defect: the hand-rolled helper
 answered 0 for every non-ASCII input whose text was the topmost allocation and
 answered correctly one allocation later, so a single-position probe reports
 whichever position it happened to use with total confidence.

  head-of : List Integer -> Integer
  head-of (xs) = if list-length xs == 0 then -999 else list-at xs 0

  units-of : Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  units-of (t) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= text-length t then acc
   else units-of t (i + 1) (acc & " " & show (char-code-at t i))

  top : Integer -> Text
  top (u) =
   let t = unicode-bytes-to-text [u]
   in let b = text-to-unicode-bytes t
   in show u & " units=[" & units-of t 0 "" & " ] n=" & show (text-length t)
      & " back=" & show (head-of b) & " cnt=" & show (list-length b)

  buried : Integer -> Text
  buried (u) =
   let t = unicode-bytes-to-text [u]
   in let filler = char-encode (code-to-char 65)
   in let b = text-to-unicode-bytes t
   in show u & " buried=" & show (head-of b) & " filler=" & show (text-length filler)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni "topmost"
   print-line-uni (top 65)
   print-line-uni (top 233)
   print-line-uni (top 1072)
   print-line-uni (top 192)
   print-line-uni (top 960)
   print-line-uni (top 8364)
   print-line-uni "buried"
   print-line-uni (buried 65)
   print-line-uni (buried 233)
   print-line-uni (buried 1072)
   print-line-uni (buried 192)
   print-line-uni (buried 960)
   print-line-uni (buried 8364)
  end
